.TH MD2MS 1
.SH NAME
md2ms \- markdown as troff -ms
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B md2ms
[
.I file ...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Md2ms
writes the markdown of its files, or of its standard input, as
.IR troff (1)
input for the
.IR ms (6)
macros.
The first heading of one
.L #
is the title
.RB ( .TL );
the others are section headings
.RB ( .SH ).
A blank line ends a paragraph
.RB ( .LP );
a line that starts with
.LR - ,
.L *
or
.L +
is a bulleted item, and one that starts with a number and a period a numbered one
.RB ( .IP ).
Inline,
.BI ** text **
is bold,
.BI * text *
italic, and
.BI ` text `
constant width.
.PP
A fenced block,
.L ```
on a line before it and after it, is set as program text
.RB ( .P1
and
.BR .P2 ),
unless its language is
.LR pic :
then it is a
.IR pic (1)
picture, between
.B .PS
and
.B .PE
if it has not its own, as
.IR sketch (1)
writes them.
.SH EXAMPLES
Render a document with a drawing in it, and look at it:
.IP
.EX
md2ms doc.md | pic | tbl | troff -ms | page
.EE
.PP
From
.IR acme 's
.IR win ,
which has no window of
.IR rio 's
for
.I page
to draw in, render it to PostScript and plumb that, which opens
.I page
in a window of its own:
.IP
.EX
md2ms doc.md | pic | tbl | troff -ms | lp -dstdout >doc.ps; plumb doc.ps
.EE
.PP
.IR Page (1)
turns
.IR troff 's
output into PostScript with
.BR "lp -dstdout" ;
here
.I lp
has no printers, and
.B -dstdout
is all it does, by
.BR aux/tr2post .
.SH SOURCE
plan9web's
.B rc/bin/md2ms
and
.B rc/bin/lp
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR ms (6),
.IR pic (1),
.IR troff (1),
.IR page (1)
.SH BUGS
Tables, links, block quotes and nested lists are set as plain text.
